        <mxCell id="n46" value="Actors are stick figures and use cases are ellipses, as required by UML.&lt;br&gt;The system boundary separates what Zoldify does from who asks for it.&lt;br&gt;Buyer-only cases sit at the top, seller-only cases at the bottom, and the&lt;br&gt;two shared cases in between, so the association lines stay short." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="1190" width="520" height="85" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
